  <div style="margin-top: 40px;">
    <div class="two-column">
      <div class="column">
        <h3 class="section-title">Reimbursement of Income Aid Payment</h3>
        <div class="content-body">
          <p>If you receive an income aid payment, you must report it as income. If you receive it in an earlier year, you can deduct the payment.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="column">
        <h3 class="section-title">Armed Forces reserves traveling more than 100 miles from home.</h3>
        <div class="content-body">
          <p>If you are a member of a reserve component of the Armed Forces, you may be able to deduct travel expenses for travel away from home. You must meet the requirements for travel expenses. See Publication 463 for more information.</p>
          <p>You are a member of a reserve component of the Armed Forces. You may be able to deduct travel expenses for travel away from home. You must meet the requirements for travel expenses. See Publication 463 for more information.</p>
        </div>
        <h3 class="section-title">Meals subject to "hours of service" limits.</h3>
        <div class="content-body">
          <p>You can deduct meals while traveling away from home, but you must meet the "hours of service" limits. You apply this 80% limit before you apply the 2% of adjusted gross income limit.</p>
        </div>
        <h3 class="section-title">Gift expenses.</h3>
        <div class="content-body">
          <p>You can generally deduct up to $25 of gift expenses to any one individual during the year. You can deduct expenses for gifts to charities.</p>
          <p>Identical, widely distributed items costing $4 or less can be deducted as a gift expense.</p>
          <p>Signs, racks, and promotional materials to be displayed on the premises of the recipient.</p>
        </div>
        <h3 class="section-title">Local lodging.</h3>
        <div class="content-body">
          <p>If your employer provides or requires you to stay in a hotel, you may not be able to deduct the lodging expense. If the lodging is if it is on a temporary basis, it is necessary for you to participate in or conduct your job. See Publication 463 for more information.</p>
        </div>
        <h3 class="section-title">Additional information.</h3>
        <div class="content-body">
          <p>See Publication 463 for more information on travel, transportation, meal, entertainment, and gift expenses, and reimbursements for these expenses.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

