  <h2 style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">How To Get Tax Help</h2>
  <p style="font-size: 10pt; margin-bottom: 20px;">You can get help with unresolved tax issues, order free publications, and ask tax questions. You can also get information from the IRS in several ways. By selecting the method that is best for you, you will have quick and easy access to tax help.</p>

  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <h3 style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">Contacting Your Taxpayer Advocate.</h3>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">The Taxpayer Advocate Service (TAS) is an independent organization within the IRS that helps taxpayers who are experiencing economic harm, who are seeking help in resolving tax problems that have not been resolved through normal channels, or who believe that an IRS procedure is incorrect or abusive.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 10px;">TAS is your voice at the IRS.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <h3 style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">Free tax services.</h3>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">To find out what services are avail-able, get publication 910, IRS Guide to Free Tax Services. This publication provides information about free tax preparation services, including tax preparation programs. It also has an index of over 100 TaxTelx topics (recorded tax information) you can listen to on your computer.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 10px;">Available versions of IRS published products are available in print and electronically.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <h3 style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">Taxpayer Advocate Service (TAS)</h3>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">TAS helps taxpayers who are experiencing economic harm, who are seeking help in resolving tax problems that have not been resolved through normal channels, or who believe that an IRS procedure is incorrect or abusive.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 10px;">TAS is your voice at the IRS.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <h3 style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">Free help with your return.</h3>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Free help in preparing your return is available through the IRS Free File program. The Volunteer Income Tax Assistance (VITA) program and the Tax Counseling for Taxpayers (TCT) program provide free tax help to taxpayers aged 60 and older with their tax returns. Many IRS sites offer free electronic filing and all volunteers will be trained to help you prepare your return. You can find more information at <span data-field="irs_website_1">{{ irs_website_1 }}</span>.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 10px;">As part of the TCT program, after the Tax-Aid volunteers have completed their training, they are available to help you prepare your return. For more information on these programs, go to <span data-field="irs_website_2">{{ irs_website_2 }}</span>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <h3 style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">Internet.</h3>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">You can access the IRS website at <span data-field="irs_website_3">{{ irs_website_3 }}</span> 24 hours a day, 7 days a week to:</p>
      <ul style="margin-top: 10px; padding-left: 20px;">
        <li>Find tax information, instructions, and publications.</li>
        <li>Search for tax questions online.</li>
        <li>Use the online Internal Revenue Code, Regulations, or other official guidance.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <h3 style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">E-file return.</h3>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Find out about commercial tax preparation and e-file services available to eligible taxpayers.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 10px;">Check the status of your 2009 refund. Go to <span data-field="irs_refund_status_link">{{ irs_refund_status_link }}</span>. To check the status of your refund, you must have your Social Security number, your filing status, and the exact dollar amount of your re-turn. If you filed Form 8379 with your return, you must also have the Form 8379 number. If you have 2009 tax return available so you can complete the refund status check, you must have your Social Security number, your filing status, and the exact dollar amount of your re-turn.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 10px;">Download forms, instructions, and publications.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 10px;">Order IRS products online.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 10px;">Search publications online by topic or keyword.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 10px;">Use the online Internal Revenue Code, Regulations, or other official guidance.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 10px;">View Internal Revenue Bulletins (IRBs) published in the last few years.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 10px;">Figure your tax liability along with the using the IRS Tax Calculator online at <span data-field="irs_tax_calculator_link">{{ irs_tax_calculator_link }}</span>.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 10px;">Determine if Form 6251 must be filed by using our Alternative Minimum Tax (AMT) Assistant.</p>
